   "he": "וּמִבְּאֵר הַקַּר. מַאי בְּאֵר הַקַּר? אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: בּוֹר שֶׁהִקְרוּ עָלֶיהָ דְּבָרִים וְהִתִּירוּהָ.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna that water may be drawn on a Festival «from the Heker Well.» The Gemara asks: «What is the Heker Well? Shmuel said:» It is «a cistern with regard to which they advanced» [«hikru»] «arguments and permitted» drawing water from «it» on a Festival, by proving that the Torah permits doing so."
